  "id": "DrugBank_DB01234 - MONDO_4095",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of B-cell Neoplasm through a chain of indications that converge on Methylprednisolone, a corticosteroid with known anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive properties. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone may indirectly influence B-cell neoplasms via its role in modulating immune responses, as it is linked to conditions like Plasmablastic Lymphoma and Chronic Beryllium Disease, both of which are associated with B-cell abnormalities. The presence of Methylprednisolone as a downstream mediator in multiple pathways underscores the potential role of corticosteroids in the development of B-cell malignancies. While the direct mechanism remains unclear, the integration of these pathways highlights the importance of corticosteroids in the regulation of immune and hematological processes, suggesting a possible role in the etiology of B-cell neoplasms.",
